a. Approach to the Project 
The project involved extending a skeleton Java program to parse a scene definition file and 
draw various graphical images based on the information contained in the file. The program 
needed to handle several shapes, including Right Triangle, Rectangle, Isosceles Triangle, 
Parallelogram, Regular Polygon, and Text. The assignment provided a skeleton program 
that already had a basic framework set up. My task was to extend it to handle new shapes 
and properly parse the scene definition file. I needed to update the Lexer to handle new 
tokens such as Isosceles, Parallelogram, Text, and others. The Parser class was then 
modified to interpret the tokens and create the appropriate shapes. I carefully handled 
coordinate parsing and ensured that properties like height, width, and color were parsed 
correctly. Each image type was handled individually in the parser with conditions based on 
the tokens. I created new classes for each of the shapes, extending a base Image class. Text 
was implemented by drawing a string on a specified location. RegularPolygon and 
SolidPolygon required calculating the coordinates of vertices based on sides and radius. 
Parallelogram and Isosceles Triangle were handled by calculating the coordinates based on 
the given dimensions and offset. After implementing the code, I tested the parsing and 
drawing functionality to ensure all new shapes were parsed correctly and displayed 
properly. 


