c. Lessons Learned and Improvements 
1. Parsing Complex Scene Files 
Handling the grammar for parsing complex scene definitions was tricky. Ensuring the 
parser interpreted the different tokens correctly (especially the images' properties) took 
careful handling of the Lexer and Parser logic. 
2. Handling Token Types 
The Lexer had to be carefully modified to account for new image types and attributes (e.g., 
TEXT, HEIGHT, WIDTH). Managing the proper flow between different tokens and validating 
them in the Parser was critical to prevent unexpected errors. 
3. Object-Oriented Design 
The design of the Image class and its subclasses (like RightTriangle, Rectangle, etc.) was 
key to maintaining clear and extendable code. Using inheritance made it easier to manage 
different types of images. 
4. Debugging 
Debugging issues like unexpected tokens was time-consuming. A clear understanding of 
the grammar and debugging information from the token output helped a lot. 
Improvements 
1. Error Handling 
The program could benefit from better error handling, particularly for invalid or missing 
fields in the scene file. A more descriptive error message would help debug issues faster. 
2. Modularization 
The program can be further modularized. For instance, the Parser class could be split into 
smaller classes to handle different image types, making the code more maintainable and 
easier to extend. 
3. Efficiency 
The Lexer could be optimized for large scene files to handle more complex parsing tasks 
more efficiently. 
4. GUI Improvements 
The current implementation is functional, but additional GUI features could be added, 
such as interactive editing of the scene, zooming, and moving objects. 


Conclusion 
This project was a great learning experience in terms of parsing and interpreting scene 
definitions in Java. It involved a combination of careful lexical analysis, object-oriented 
design, and debugging techniques. By following a structured approach, I was able to extend 
the program to handle additional image types and successfully parse complex scene files. 
